WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:03.388
- [Narrator] Bessie,
Olive, Sally, and Jess

00:00:03.388 --> 00:00:05.805
have one big thing in common.

00:00:06.828 --> 00:00:08.578
(cow mooing)

00:00:08.578 --> 00:00:10.161
They all love jazz.

00:00:11.576 --> 00:00:15.743
(lively jazz music)
(cow mooing)

00:00:21.114 --> 00:00:23.216
This is Live Oak, Florida,

00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:25.604
a small town west of Jacksonville,

00:00:25.604 --> 00:00:27.932
not the type of place
you associate with jazz,

00:00:27.932 --> 00:00:29.599
and yet, there's Ed.

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:32.729
- [Ed] I'm a dairy farmer
here in north Florida,

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:34.812
home to about 6,800 cows.

00:00:36.511 --> 00:00:39.308
- [Narrator] That Ed, he can really blow.

00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:41.729
He's been playing trombone
since elementary school,

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:44.860
but his audience has changed.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.360
This is his story.

00:00:48.258 --> 00:00:50.797
- The first time I can
remember the cows coming up

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:53.056
is I was just standing out in the backyard

00:00:53.056 --> 00:00:56.386
and playing a trombone, and all the cows

00:00:56.386 --> 00:00:57.968
came up to the fence.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.311
I had a full audience.

00:00:59.311 --> 00:01:00.556
(Ed laughs)

00:01:00.556 --> 00:01:02.667
They're not particularly critical either.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.188
Cows are very much creatures of habit.

00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:07.567
The music is something
that's out of the norm

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.699
and that's why they're entertained.

00:01:09.699 --> 00:01:12.778
The cows have an ability to understand

00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:14.154
what's threatening and what's pleasing,

00:01:14.154 --> 00:01:17.487
and music is definitely pleasing to 'em.

00:01:18.652 --> 00:01:22.767
I have no idea if it's the
one heifer heard the music

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.065
and the rest of 'em are
following the other heifer,

00:01:26.065 --> 00:01:27.187
but it really doesn't matter.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:30.107
At the end of the day, we're
all having a good time.

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:32.376
(trombone music)
(cow mooing)

00:01:32.376 --> 00:01:35.134
My dad told me when we were kids, he said,

00:01:35.134 --> 00:01:39.045
"It's important from day one
how we take care of animals."

00:01:39.045 --> 00:01:41.493
And we like to consider
ourselves good stewards

00:01:41.493 --> 00:01:43.551
of the land and good
stewards of the animals,

00:01:43.551 --> 00:01:45.480
and playing the trombone
is not any different

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.921
than going out and how we feed our cows,

00:01:47.921 --> 00:01:50.951
and we take care of our cows,
it's all about our interaction

00:01:50.951 --> 00:01:52.253
with these animals.

00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:56.370
Our animals, they care, and
so you play music to 'em,

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.203
they'll remember that.

00:02:02.184 --> 00:02:04.767
(chiming note)

